---
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-GB">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="description" content="Learn about The Wonder Years Day Nursery in Wednesbury, caring for children since 1994 with an experienced team, flexible childcare and an individual approach to every child." />
    <title>About The Wonder Years Day Nursery | Wednesbury</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href={`${base}styles/global.css`} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
    <div class="wireframe-banner">About The Wonder Years · Content and image placement for review</div>
    <SiteHeader current="about" />

    <main id="main">
      <section class="section hero">
        <div class="container hero-grid">
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p class="eyebrow">Caring for children since 1994</p>
            <h1>About The Wonder Years</h1>
            <p class="lead">The Wonder Years Day Nursery has been caring for children in Wednesbury since 1994.</p>
            <p>From babies taking their first steps into nursery life to older children returning during the school holidays, the nursery has grown around one central idea: children should be cared for as individuals, in a place where they can feel safe, known and supported.</p>
            <p>Today, that means combining experienced childcare with a flexible approach to family life, close relationships with parents and care that adapts as children grow.</p>
            <div class="button-row">
              <a class="button" href={`${base}meet-the-team/`}>Meet the team</a>
              <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}contact/#enquiry`}>Arrange a nursery visit</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="image-placeholder hero-image" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for a welcoming photograph of The Wonder Years nursery">
            <span>Nursery exterior image placeholder</span>
            <small>The building, entrance or another recognisable part of the setting</small>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-muted">
        <div class="container split-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Part of Wednesbury for over 30 years</p>
            <h2>Caring for children since 1994</h2>
            <p>The Wonder Years was established in 1994 by Hilary Walker and has been part of the Wednesbury community for more than 30 years.</p>
            <p>Over that time, generations of children and families have come through the nursery doors, while the setting itself has continued to develop around the changing needs of children and parents.</p>
            <p>The nursery now cares for children from <strong>six weeks old</strong>, with separate spaces for babies, toddlers and preschool children, as well as school-holiday care for children up to Year 6.</p>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}rooms/`}>Explore our rooms</a>
          </div>
          <div class="funded-hours-card">
            <p class="eyebrow">Our approach</p>
            <h3>Flexible, reliable and centred on each child</h3>
            <p>Children are not expected to fit one standard routine. The team takes time to understand each child’s:</p>
            <ul>
              <li>personality and interests;</li>
              <li>routines and communication;</li>
              <li>stage of development; and</li>
              <li>individual care and learning needs.</li>
            </ul>
            <p>This understanding shapes settling in, mealtimes, play, learning, rest and preparation for the next stage.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container split-grid reverse">
          <div class="image-placeholder landscape" role="img" aria-label="Placeholder for a current group photograph of nursery staff">
            <span>Nursery team image placeholder</span>
            <small>A current group photograph or natural image of several team members</small>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Experience and continuity</p>
            <h2>A team with experience behind it</h2>
            <p>The Wonder Years is led by Nursery Manager <strong>Mandy Barker</strong>, who joined the nursery in 2007, alongside Deputy Manager <strong>Sarah Avery</strong>, who has been part of the nursery since 2003.</p>
            <p>Across the wider team, a number of practitioners have worked at The Wonder Years for well over a decade. That continuity gives children familiar adults around them and means newer staff work alongside colleagues with substantial experience of the nursery, its families and early years care.</p>
            <p>The team brings together different qualifications, experience and backgrounds across the baby, toddler and preschool rooms and wider support roles.</p>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}meet-the-team/`}>Meet the team</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-accent">
        <div class="container split-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">A home from home</p>
            <h2>A place where children can feel known</h2>
            <p>For The Wonder Years, a home from home is less about making nursery identical to home and more about creating the familiarity, relationships and understanding that help children feel secure.</p>
            <p>Children spend their days with staff who get to know them, their routines and the things that interest them.</p>
            <p>Key people and the wider room teams work with parents and carers so that nursery life reflects the child in front of them rather than following the same pattern for everyone.</p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Learning through everyday life</p>
            <h2>Care and learning are closely connected</h2>
            <p>The nursery follows the <strong>Early Years Foundation Stage</strong> and is informed by <strong>Birth to 5 Matters</strong>, but learning does not happen only during planned activities.</p>
            <p>Children develop through play, stories, conversation, creativity, movement, relationships, everyday routines, growing independence and the interests they bring with them.</p>
            <p>Staff observe children’s progress and use what they know about each child to plan appropriate experiences and next steps.</p>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}learning-development/`}>Learning and Development</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section">
        <div class="container split-grid">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Working with families</p>
            <h2>Keeping parents connected</h2>
            <p>Parents and carers are encouraged to talk to the team about their child’s routines, development, interests and any support they may need.</p>
            <p>The <strong>Famly app</strong> also helps families stay connected with their child’s day, with updates that can include meals, sleep, nappies, activities, photographs, videos and learning observations.</p>
            <p>That communication continues at drop-off and collection, when staff are available to share information and answer questions.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="funded-hours-card">
            <p class="eyebrow">Care around family life</p>
            <h3>Practical and flexible childcare</h3>
            <ul>
              <li>childcare from six weeks old;</li>
              <li>full-day, five-hour and hourly sessions;</li>
              <li>funded childcare for eligible families from nine months;</li>
              <li>school-holiday care up to Year 6;</li>
              <li>year-round opening apart from bank holidays, Christmas Eve and New Year’s Eve; and</li>
              <li>settling in at each child’s pace.</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}fees-funding-joining/`}>Funding and Joining</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section section-muted">
        <div class="container funding-panel">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Safety, inclusion and individual support</p>
            <h2>Every child supported to take part</h2>
            <p>Children’s safety and wellbeing sit at the centre of nursery life.</p>
            <p>The nursery has named safeguarding leads and a SENDCO, and staff receive safeguarding training alongside ongoing updates.</p>
            <p>Children with additional needs are supported as individuals, with care and learning adapted where needed so they can participate in nursery life alongside their peers.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="button-stack">
            <a class="button" href={`${base}safeguarding-send-inclusion/`}>Safeguarding, SEND and Inclusion</a>
            <a class="button button-secondary" href={`${base}contact/`}>Speak to the nursery</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="final-cta">
        <div class="container">
          <h2>Come and see The Wonder Years</h2>
          <p>A visit gives you a much better sense of the environment, the rooms and the people who will be caring for your child.</p>
          <p>You are welcome to arrange a nursery tour, meet the team and talk through the childcare you are looking for.</p>
          <div class="button-row centred">
            <a class="button button-light" href={`${base}contact/#enquiry`}>Arrange a nursery visit</a>
            <a class="button button-outline-light" href="tel:01215566979">Call 0121 556 6979</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <SiteFooter />
  </body>
</html>
